[{"category":"section","location":"validation/#Validation-and-Benchmark-with-PySPEDAS","page":"Validation and Benchmark","text":"We compare ELFINData results against PySPEDAS to ensure numerical parity and to track performance. The following benchmarks illustrate the typical workflow.\n\nState variable ELA_POS_GEI: Julia is about 200 times faster than Python for this retrieval.\n\nusing PySPEDAS\nusing ELFINData\nusing Chairmarks\n\ntrange = (\"2021-08-08\", \"2021-08-10\")\nela_pos_gei = ELA_POS_GEI(trange)\npy_ela_pos_gei = Array(PySPEDAS.elfin.state(trange).ela_pos_gei)\n@assert ela_pos_gei == py_ela_pos_gei'\n@b Array(ELA_POS_GEI(trange)), PySPEDAS.elfin.state(trange), pyspedas.projects.elfin.state(trange)\n\nProcessing EPD L2 spectra: Julia is about 100 times faster than Python for spectral derivations across the same interval.\n\ntrange = (\"2020-10-01\", \"2020-10-02\")\nnflux_para = epd_spectral(trange).para\npy_nflux_para = PySPEDAS.elfin.epd(trange; level = \"l2\").ela_pef_hs_nflux_para\n@assert nflux_para ≈ Array(py_nflux_para)'\nb1 = @b epd_spectral($trange)\nb2 = @b PySPEDAS.elfin.epd($trange; level = \"l2\")\n@info \"Julia\" b1\n@info \"PySPEDAS\" b2\n\nnote: Array layout\nJulia arrays follow the column-major convention used by most CDF files (time is the last dimension), whereas NumPy and PySPEDAS use row-major arrays (time is the first dimension). Transpose the PySPEDAS output before comparing so the dimensions align.","title":"Validation and Benchmark with PySPEDAS"},{"category":"section","location":"#ELFINData","page":"Home","text":"(Image: DOI) (Image: version)\n\nELFINData.jl provides a high-level Julia interface to the ELFIN mission's particle and field measurements. The sections below highlight the most common entry points and link to the auto-generated API reference.","title":"ELFINData"},{"category":"section","location":"#Installation","page":"Home","text":"using Pkg\nPkg.add(\"ELFINData\")\n\nAn agent skill is included for using ELFINData with natural language. To install it using skills, run:\n\nnpx skills add JuliaSpacePhysics/ELFINData.jl","title":"Installation"},{"category":"section","location":"#Quick-Start","page":"Home","text":"The examples in this section walk through the typical workflow: discover an instrument's datasets, load data for the specified time range, and request processed data products.\n\nusing ELFINData\n\n# Inspect the Energetic Particle Detector (EPD) datasets\nEPD.datasets\n\nFrom the Julia REPL you can also type ?EPD to view the EPD documentation.\n\n# Load the instrument's datasets (using the logical source name is the most portable approach)\nELA_L1_FGS(\"2020-10-01\", \"2020-10-02\")\n# Alternatively, specify probe and datatype explicitly. This resolves the same logical dataset.\n# If no time range is given, the call returns the set of datasets (i.e. `FGM(; probe = \"a\", datatype = \"survey\") == ELA_L1_FGS`)\nFGM(\"2020-10-01\", \"2020-10-02\"; probe = \"a\", datatype = \"survey\")\n\nThe following function derives directionally resolved flux spectra (omni, para, anti) and/or pitch-angle spectra from EPD level 2 data with a single call.\n\nepd_spectral(\"2020-10-01\", \"2020-10-02\"; probe = \"a\")\n\nCommonly used variables have concise convenience wrappers. Because these variables are uniquely named, no additional metadata (such as probe, datatype, level, or dataset) is required to access them.\n\nELA_POS_GEI(\"2020-10-01\", \"2020-10-02\")\n# Alternative ways to access the same variable: \n# `STATE(\"2020-10-01\", \"2020-10-02\"; probe = \"a\")[\"ela_pos_gei\"]` or\n# `ELA_L1_STATE(\"2020-10-01\", \"2020-10-02\")[\"ela_pos_gei\"]`\n\nELB_FGS(\"2020-10-01\", \"2020-10-02\")\n# Alternative ways to access the same variable: \n# `ELB_L1_FGS(\"2020-10-01\", \"2020-10-02\")[\"elb_fgs\"]` or \n# `FGM(\"2020-10-01\", \"2020-10-02\"; probe = \"b\", datatype = \"survey\")[\"elb_fgs\"]`\n\nELA_PEF_HS_EPAT_NFLUX(\"2020-10-01\", \"2020-10-02\")\n# Alternative ways to access the same variable: \n# `ELA_L2_EPDEF(\"2020-10-01\", \"2020-10-02\")[\"ela_pef_hs_Epat_nflux\"]` or \n# `EPD(\"2020-10-01\", \"2020-10-02\"; probe = \"a\", level = \"l2\", datatype = \"epdef\")[\"ela_pef_hs_Epat_nflux\"]`","title":"Quick Start"},{"category":"section","location":"#Quick-Plots","page":"Home","text":"using ELFINData\nusing Dates\nusing ELFINData.DimensionalData\nusing SpacePhysicsMakie, WGLMakie\nusing Bonito # hide\nPage() # hide\n\n# https://data.elfin.ucla.edu/ela/overplots/2022/09/05/ela_l2_overview_20220905_10_ndes.gif\nt0 = DateTime(\"2022-09-05T10:00:00\")\nt1 = DateTime(\"2022-09-05T10:30:00\")\n\n# Example: plot EPD flux spectra\nspectra = epd_spectral(t0, t1; probe = \"a\")[Ti(t0 .. t1)]\ntplot(degap.([spectra.omni, spectra.anti, spectra.perp, spectra.para]); colormap=:turbo)","title":"Quick Plots"},{"category":"section","location":"#API","page":"Home","text":"","title":"API"},{"category":"section","location":"#Instruments","page":"Home","text":"","title":"Instruments"},{"category":"section","location":"#Datasets","page":"Home","text":"","title":"Datasets"},{"category":"section","location":"#Variables","page":"Home","text":"","title":"Variables"},{"category":"section","location":"#Functions-and-Types","page":"Home","text":"","title":"Functions and Types"},{"category":"module","location":"#ELFINData.ELFINData","page":"Home","text":"Load and process data from the Electron Losses and Fields INvestigation (ELFIN) mission.\n\nInstruments\n\nFluxgate Magnetometer (FGM)\nEnergetic Particle Detector (EPD)\nMagneto Resistive Magnetometer-a (MRMa)\nMagneto Resistive Magnetometer-i (MRMi)\nState data (state)\nEngineering data (ENG)\n\nFunctions\n\nepd_spectral: Load ELFIN EPD L2 data and extract directionally resolved flux spectra (omni, para, anti) and/or pitch angle spectra.\n\nReferences: Website, NASA Science, Wikipedia, DOI\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"ELFINData.ELFINData"},{"category":"constant","location":"#ELFINData.EPD","page":"Home","text":"Energetic Particle Detector (EPD)\n\nThe EPD consists of two heads: an electron head that measures 50 keV to 5 MeV electrons and an ion head that measures 50 to 5000 keV ions.\n\nDatasets: \n\nELFIN A: ELA_L1_EPDEF, ELA_L1_EPDIF, ELA_L2_EPDEF\nELFIN B: ELB_L1_EPDEF, ELB_L1_EPDIF, ELB_L2_EPDEF\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"ELFINData.EPD"},{"category":"constant","location":"#ELFINData.FGM","page":"Home","text":"Fluxgate Magnetometer (FGM)\n\nDatasets: ELA_L1_FGS, ELB_L1_FGS\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"ELFINData.FGM"},{"category":"constant","location":"#ELFINData.STATE","page":"Home","text":"State data (STATE)\n\nDatasets: ELA_L1_STATE, ELB_L1_STATE\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"ELFINData.STATE"},{"category":"constant","location":"#ELFINData.ELA_L1_EPDEF","page":"Home","text":"ELFIN A L1 EPD Electron Counts (Version 1)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"ELFINData.ELA_L1_EPDEF"},{"category":"constant","location":"#ELFINData.ELA_L1_EPDIF","page":"Home","text":"ELFIN A L1 EPD Ion Counts (Version 1)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"ELFINData.ELA_L1_EPDIF"},{"category":"constant","location":"#ELFINData.ELA_L1_FGS","page":"Home","text":"ELFIN A L1 FGM Survey (Version 1)\n\nMain data variables: ELA_FGS\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"ELFINData.ELA_L1_FGS"},{"category":"constant","location":"#ELFINData.ELA_L1_MRMA","page":"Home","text":"ELFIN A L1 MRMA (Version 1)\n\nMain data variables: ELA_MRMA\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"ELFINData.ELA_L1_MRMA"},{"category":"constant","location":"#ELFINData.ELA_L1_MRMI","page":"Home","text":"ELFIN A L1 MRMI (Version 1)\n\nMain data variables: ELA_MRMI\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"ELFINData.ELA_L1_MRMI"},{"category":"constant","location":"#ELFINData.ELA_L1_STATE","page":"Home","text":"ELFIN A L1 State (Version 2)\n\nMain data variables: ELA_POS_GEI\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"ELFINData.ELA_L1_STATE"},{"category":"constant","location":"#ELFINData.ELA_L2_EPDEF","page":"Home","text":"ELFIN A L2 EPD Electron Counts (Version 1)\n\nMain data variables: ELA_PEF_HS_EPAT_NFLUX, ELA_PEF_FS_EPAT_NFLUX, ELA_PEF_HS_EPAT_EFLUX, ELA_PEF_FS_EPAT_EFLUX\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"ELFINData.ELA_L2_EPDEF"},{"category":"constant","location":"#ELFINData.ELB_L1_EPDEF","page":"Home","text":"ELFIN B L1 EPD Electron Counts (Version 1)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"ELFINData.ELB_L1_EPDEF"},{"category":"constant","location":"#ELFINData.ELB_L1_EPDIF","page":"Home","text":"ELFIN B L1 EPD Ion Counts (Version 1)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"ELFINData.ELB_L1_EPDIF"},{"category":"constant","location":"#ELFINData.ELB_L1_FGS","page":"Home","text":"ELFIN B L1 FGM Survey (Version 1)\n\nMain data variables: ELB_FGS\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"ELFINData.ELB_L1_FGS"},{"category":"constant","location":"#ELFINData.ELB_L1_MRMA","page":"Home","text":"ELFIN B L1 MRMA (Version 1)\n\nMain data variables: ELB_MRMA\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"ELFINData.ELB_L1_MRMA"},{"category":"constant","location":"#ELFINData.ELB_L1_MRMI","page":"Home","text":"ELFIN B L1 MRMI (Version 1)\n\nMain data variables: ELB_MRMI\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"ELFINData.ELB_L1_MRMI"},{"category":"constant","location":"#ELFINData.ELB_L1_STATE","page":"Home","text":"ELFIN B L1 State (Version 2)\n\nMain data variables: ELB_POS_GEI\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"ELFINData.ELB_L1_STATE"},{"category":"constant","location":"#ELFINData.ELB_L2_EPDEF","page":"Home","text":"ELFIN B L2 EPD Electron Counts (Version 1)\n\nMain data variables: ELB_PEF_HS_EPAT_NFLUX, ELB_PEF_FS_EPAT_NFLUX, ELB_PEF_HS_EPAT_EFLUX, ELB_PEF_FS_EPAT_EFLUX\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"ELFINData.ELB_L2_EPDEF"},{"category":"constant","location":"#ELFINData.ELA_FGS","page":"Home","text":"ELFIN A FGM Magnetic field B in XYZ Sensor Coordinates, Survey Mode\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"ELFINData.ELA_FGS"},{"category":"constant","location":"#ELFINData.ELA_MRMA","page":"Home","text":"Magnetic field XYZ Sensor data collected by ACB, Sensor Coordinates, ADC units\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"ELFINData.ELA_MRMA"},{"category":"constant","location":"#ELFINData.ELA_MRMI","page":"Home","text":"Magnetic field XYZ Sensor data collected by IDPU, Sensor Coordinates, ADC units\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"ELFINData.ELA_MRMI"},{"category":"constant","location":"#ELFINData.ELA_PEF_FS_EPAT_EFLUX","page":"Home","text":"ELFIN A EnergyPitchAngleTime spectra eflux, full spin resolution\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"ELFINData.ELA_PEF_FS_EPAT_EFLUX"},{"category":"constant","location":"#ELFINData.ELA_PEF_FS_EPAT_NFLUX","page":"Home","text":"ELFIN A EnergyPitchAngleTime spectra nflux, full spin resolution\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"ELFINData.ELA_PEF_FS_EPAT_NFLUX"},{"category":"constant","location":"#ELFINData.ELA_PEF_HS_EPAT_EFLUX","page":"Home","text":"ELFIN A EnergyPitchAngleTime spectra eflux, half spin resolution\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"ELFINData.ELA_PEF_HS_EPAT_EFLUX"},{"category":"constant","location":"#ELFINData.ELA_PEF_HS_EPAT_NFLUX","page":"Home","text":"ELFIN A EnergyPitchAngleTime spectra nflux, half spin resolution\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"ELFINData.ELA_PEF_HS_EPAT_NFLUX"},{"category":"constant","location":"#ELFINData.ELA_POS_GEI","page":"Home","text":"ELFIN A State Position XYZ in GEI coordinates\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"ELFINData.ELA_POS_GEI"},{"category":"constant","location":"#ELFINData.ELB_FGS","page":"Home","text":"ELFIN B FGM Magnetic field B in XYZ Sensor Coordinates, Survey Mode\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"ELFINData.ELB_FGS"},{"category":"constant","location":"#ELFINData.ELB_MRMA","page":"Home","text":"Magnetic field XYZ Sensor data collected by ACB, Sensor Coordinates, ADC units\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"ELFINData.ELB_MRMA"},{"category":"constant","location":"#ELFINData.ELB_MRMI","page":"Home","text":"Magnetic field XYZ Sensor data collected by IDPU, Sensor Coordinates, ADC units\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"ELFINData.ELB_MRMI"},{"category":"constant","location":"#ELFINData.ELB_PEF_FS_EPAT_EFLUX","page":"Home","text":"ELFIN B EnergyPitchAngleTime spectra eflux, full spin resolution\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"ELFINData.ELB_PEF_FS_EPAT_EFLUX"},{"category":"constant","location":"#ELFINData.ELB_PEF_FS_EPAT_NFLUX","page":"Home","text":"ELFIN B EnergyPitchAngleTime spectra nflux, full spin resolution\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"ELFINData.ELB_PEF_FS_EPAT_NFLUX"},{"category":"constant","location":"#ELFINData.ELB_PEF_HS_EPAT_EFLUX","page":"Home","text":"ELFIN B EnergyPitchAngleTime spectra eflux, half spin resolution\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"ELFINData.ELB_PEF_HS_EPAT_EFLUX"},{"category":"constant","location":"#ELFINData.ELB_PEF_HS_EPAT_NFLUX","page":"Home","text":"ELFIN B EnergyPitchAngleTime spectra nflux, half spin resolution\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"ELFINData.ELB_PEF_HS_EPAT_NFLUX"},{"category":"constant","location":"#ELFINData.ELB_POS_GEI","page":"Home","text":"ELFIN B State Position XYZ in GEI coordinates\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"ELFINData.ELB_POS_GEI"},{"category":"method","location":"#ELFINData.epd_spectral-Tuple","page":"Home","text":"epd_spectral(trange; probe = \"a\", type = \"nflux\", datatype = \"epdef\", fullspin = false)\n\nLoad ELFIN EPD L2 data and process it to extract directionally resolved flux spectra (omni, para, anti) and/or pitch angle spectra.\n\nReturns a NamedTuple-like container with omni, para, anti, and prec flux spectra.\n\nepd_spectral(\"2020-10-01\", \"2020-10-02\")\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"ELFINData.epd_spectral"}]
